{"seq":1,"mint":"C27","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"`search_key` stores world_root's own spelling as the key whenever the search root and the worktree root name the same directory","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F6","F18","F21"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"    let same = fs::canonicalize(root)\n        .ok()\n        .zip(fs::canonicalize(world_root).ok())\n        .map(|(a, b)| a == b)\n        .unwrap_or(false);\n    if same { world_root.to_string() } else { resolved }","why":"The key uses world_root's spelling only when both canonicalizations succeed and compare equal. If canonicalization fails, the code chooses `resolved` instead, so the asserted “whenever” does not hold.","quoted":true}],"at":1790153589,"cost":0.005408597,"elapsed_ms":24382,"attempts":3,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":1,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1,"typed_classify_calls":1,"typed_literal_calls":0}
